  "description": "Months (1-12) in which fruit, vegetables and nuts come from Italian production. 'harvest' = fresh domestic season (field, protected cultivation, or citrus picked from the tree); 'storage' = Italian crop sold from storage. The underlying Italian calendars only list months of availability; the split into harvest and storage was added by FoodMission for storable crops (apple, pear, kiwi, potato, onion, garlic, pumpkin, walnut). Items with domestic=false are imported only. Items not listed are not covered by the sources (no data), not necessarily imported.",
  "source": "Compiled by FoodMission. Primary source: the seasonality table (Tabella 12, 'Calendario della stagionalità dei prodotti ortofrutticoli') in the Regione Friuli Venezia Giulia school-catering guidelines, transcribed for the fruit and vegetables it covers. Items it does not cover were taken from the seasonality calendars of the Regione Abruzzo school-catering guidelines (DGR annex, BURA 2023) and the Comune di Gaiole in Chianti (Siena), supplemented by well-established knowledge for the harvest/storage split and for a few conflicting entries. None of these documents states an open reuse licence; they are public-administration publications (official acts are excluded from copyright under art. 5 of Italian Law 633/1941, but the FVG booklet is not clearly an official act). The import-only list was added by FoodMission.",
